WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.458
STEPHANIE WONG:
Today we're talking

00:00:01.458 --> 00:00:04.680
about Apigee wins, our
commitment to EU customers,

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.960
and VM fleet-wide monitoring.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.390
I'm Stephanie Wong, and
welcome to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.460
where we serve you
the lowest latency

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.650
news from the safety of home.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.520
APIs let developers easily
access, combine, and share

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.730
valuable data and functionality,
helping companies adapt

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.800
to disruption and reinvent.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.260
So partnering with the
right API management vendor

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.600
is critical to
building and scaling

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.710
a successful API program.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.280
We're excited to share
that Gartner has recognized

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.670
Google Apigee as a
leader in the 2020 Magic

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.700
Quadrant for full
lifecycle API management,

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.580
marking the fifth time in a row
we've earned this recognition.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.700
In this year's report,
Apigee is placed

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.090
highest among all the vendors
for the ability to execute.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.770
Congrats team.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:53.010
In recent months, European
customers and policymakers

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.940
have placed even more emphasis
on working with cloud providers

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.090
to protect customers' most
sensitive information.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.830
Google Cloud has
partnered with them

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:05.190
to make significant progress
to delivering more capabilities

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.760
for strict data security
and privacy requirements.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.360
They reflect three distinct
pillars of data, operational,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.430
and software sovereignty.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:16.800
Read Thomas Kurian's
announcement in the blog

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.080
post to learn more.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:22.850
You can now monitor your compute
VM fleet's health all together.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.190
The new single pane of
glass infrastructure summary

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:28.460
dashboard lets you see
aggregate fleet-wide statistics

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.800
at a glance, and
provides insight

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.240
into the top VMs for a select
group of key CPU, disk, memory,

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.578
and network metrics.

00:01:36.578 --> 00:01:37.870
Jumpstart your troubleshooting.

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.425
No setup required.

00:01:39.425 --> 00:01:41.300
Check out the blog post
to learn all about it

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.250
and try it out for yourself.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.530
Finally, the director
of product management

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:47.300
of artificial
intelligence has just

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:52.010
announced that PyTorch XLA
support for Cloud TPUs is now

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.490
generally available.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.510
This means PyTorch users
can access large scale,

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:59.000
low cost TPU
hardware accelerators

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.720
using a stable, well-supported
PyTorch integration.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.600
Google Cloud supports a
growing set of open source

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.750
implementations of widely
used deep learning models

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.430
and associated tutorials.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:14.207
Check out our post for tutorials
and how to get started.

00:02:14.207 --> 00:02:16.290
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:19.030
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.820
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.410
We'll see you in the cloud.

